{; THE ONE LIMIT. Time, and nothing else: sci counts no steps and has no
 ; step concept, so a wall-clock deadline read at every interpreted fn
 ; body entrance is the whole mechanism (reference-code/sci/doc/
 ; interrupt.md:23-35). :seon.eval/fn-entries is RECORDED beside it and
 ; is never a limit — 271M entries in 500ms reads as a spin, 12 reads as
 ; blocked in a host call.
 :seon.sci.eval/time-limit-ms [:int {:min 1}]
 ; sci's own word for an interpreter context; forked per evaluation so
 ; one eval's defs cannot reach another's.
 :seon.sci.eval/ctx [:fn {:gen/gen seon.sci.eval/ctx-generator} seon.sci.eval/ctx?]
 :seon.sci.eval/request [:map {:closed true} [:seon.cluster.run.form/source :seon.cluster.run.form/source] [:seon.sci.admit/caps :seon.sci.admit/caps] [:seon.sci.eval/time-limit-ms :seon.sci.eval/time-limit-ms] [:seon.sci.eval/ctx {:optional true} :seon.sci.eval/ctx]]
 ; What one evaluation leaves behind: a status the receipt stores, the
 ; admitted value the loop reads a disposition out of, the printed
 ; projection, and the diagnostics. Nothing here is optional-by-nil —
 ; an absent key means the evaluation had no such thing.
 :seon.sci.eval/evaluation [:map {:closed true} [:seon.cluster.eval/status :seon.cluster.eval/status] [:seon.sci.admit/value :any] [:seon.cluster.eval/result-edn :seon.cluster.eval/result-edn] [:seon.cluster.eval/error {:optional true} :seon.cluster.eval/error] [:seon.sci.admit/capped? :seon.sci.admit/capped?] [:seon.sci.admit/record :seon.sci.admit/record]]}
